Elven equipment is all non-metalic.  In a case like "elven leather
helmet" it is obvious from the name, but none of the other elven
equipment is made from metal either.  Fooproof an elven dagger or
elven broadsword and look very closely at its description.  It will
say "fireproof" not "rustproof".  Somehow elves make their weapons
out of wood.

Anyways, as you move deeper you'll start encountering plenty of
elves and some of them will leave you reasonable armor in their
wills.  It isn't all that bad to start out with a bunch of iron
dwarvish equipment coming out of the mines and have the intention
of switching to elven equivalents as soon as each individual type
of armor is encountered.  Helmet, cloak, boots, shield, though
you'll want to avoid shields from the start if you want a lot of
spellcasting.

